        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "328e1522-a31d-511c-8d93-e3b9954118fc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edward Henry “Butch” O’Hare\n- Products: USS O'Hare (DD/DDR-889)\n- Roles: Lieutenant Commander, American naval aviator\n- Organizations: United States Navy\n- Concepts: Medal of Honor, flying ace\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Henry “Butch” O’Hare was born on March 13, 1914.\n- On February 20, 1942, Lieutenant Commander Edward Henry “Butch” O’Hare of the United States Navy became the Navy’s first flying ace by single-handedly attacking a formation of nine heavy bombers approaching his aircraft carrier.\n- On April 21, 1942, Edward Henry “Butch” O’Hare became the first naval recipient of the Medal of Honor in World War II.\n- Edward Henry “Butch” O’Hare was shot down at Tarawa on November 26, 1943.\n- USS O'Hare (DD/DDR-889) was a Gearing-class destroyer of the United States Navy named for Lieutenant Commander Edward Henry “Butch” O’Hare.\n- Edward Henry “Butch” O’Hare died on November 26, 1943.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
